From b0ba4b9db609b84ab3556ab8b0419edcad274fb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Christian F.K. Schaller" <christian.schaller@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 15:25:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] scanner: List a scanner once however many drivers find it,
 and know which are for film

A network printer is found by both an eSCL and a vendor driver, and the vendor
one may not be able to open it. The helper now says which physical scanner a
device is, by USB bus address or network host. The portal gives such scanners
one id, offers the dialog one entry, ranks the drivers and opens the scanner
with the next one when the best cannot.

SANE's device type does not say which scanners are for film: one driver calls a
Plustek OpticFilm a film scanner and another a flatbed. The portal has a list
of film scanners and flatbeds with a transparency unit, and assumes that a
scanner it does not know to be for film only is for documents, so capabilities
can be used to filter. SelectScanners also takes any_capabilities.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 data/org.freedesktop.portal.Scanner.xml |  23 +-
 src/scanner-devices.h                   |  71 +++++++
 src/scanner-helper.c                    | 100 +++++++++
 src/scanner.c                           | 269 +++++++++++++++++++++---
 4 files changed, 438 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 src/scanner-devices.h

